              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ojalá hables español means “I hope you speak Spanish” or “May you speak Spanish.” Ojalá expresses the wish by itself. It needs neither a main verb nor que before the subjunctive. Keep the first frame tiny:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ojalá + subjunctive."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is a usable modern pattern. It does not make the Arabic source phrase new Spanish vocabulary."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The wish-word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The Real Academia Española records ojalá from Hispanic Arabic wa šá lláh, “and God has willed.” Long contact in al-Andalus carried the expression into Spanish, where its sound and grammatical life changed. You met another Arabic-derived function word in hasta. The historical phrase explains a route; only modern ojalá is available for your Spanish sentences."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Use only modern ojalá as the Spanish trigger."
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C18-ojala-trigger",
              "prompt": "Say 'I hope you speak Spanish' to one friend using ojalá.",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-LEX-OJALA-SUBJUNCTIVE-TRIGGER",
                "ES-GRAMMAR-AR-SUBJUNCTIVE-SINGULAR",
                "ES-LEX-HABLAR",
                "ES-LEX-ESPANOL"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 9,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "ojalá hables español.",
                "ojalá hables español",
                "ojala hables espanol"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Right: Ojalá hables español.",
                "incorrect": "Use ojalá directly before the tú subjunctive hables."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C18-ojala-no-que",
              "prompt": "Does the learned ojalá frame require que before hables? Answer yes or no.",
